<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aaron</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, Aaron was an Israelite prophet, high priest and elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a>; information about him comes only from religious texts. Exodus relates that he served as Moses' spokesman before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaoh</a>. Part of the Law given at Sinai granted the priesthood to him and his male descendants, and the kohanim are traditionally held to descend from him. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bible">Bible</a> tells how he made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-calf">golden calf</a>, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a> attributes it to Samiri. Numbers says he died aged 123 on Mount Hor, whereas Deuteronomy places his death at Moseroth. Many historians think Aaronide families did not control the priesthood before the Babylonian exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aaron.jpg" alt="Aaron" width="330" height="568" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aaron_in_Dura_Europos_synagogue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
